  "title": "androiddump: Don't pass a SOCKET as nfds to select on Win32",
  "description": "The Win32 winsock API indicates that it ignores the nfds parameter,\nwhich \"is only included for compatiblity with Berkeley sockets.\"\nThe parameter is an int, just like in UN*X.\n\nHowever, the Win32 SOCKET type is 64 bits (even though in practice\nonly the 32 bits are used; this is just beause it's a pointer\napparently), causing MSVC to complain about possibly discarding data.\nOn Win32 can either cast the SOCKET to an int to be ignored,\nor pass any integer literal (like 0) to be ignored.",
